I've been playing elven rangers exclusively recently - 122 to be
precise.

Rangers are a peculiar bunch. My strat for a ranger is to immediately
quiver my +0 arrows, saving the +2 ones for tougher monsters or later
in the game. I plunge into the mines immediately, and by level 6 or 7
my elven dagger can usually kill gnomes in 1 hit. At any rate, I eat
corpses (gnomes, dwarves, rothes, newts, whatever) in the mines and I
note that it's oh-so-easy to get a nice stack of daggers for throwing.
At that point you can switch to daggers and use arrows as a backup
until you get your diana's bow, or build a stack of elven daggers too.
The great thing about a ranger is that at range they're nearly
invincible. Even at level 3 or 4, if you're facing down 2 or 3
dwarves, 4 or 5 gnomes, a couple of rothes, etc. as long as there's 2
or 3 spaces between you and the monsters, you can and will kill them
all with your bow and arrows.

The way I die with my ranger is usually because something which I
*should* be ranging gets in melee range. You want some examples? In my
top 10 rangers I have:
death by a blue jelly (I KNOW.. I KNOW...)
death by brainlessness (cursed scroll of genocide)
a guard (i walked back to the room instead of dropping the gold first)
an invisible hobbit (don't ask)
three deaths to low-end monsters hitting me while helpless
the usual quasit, mumak, and leracotta, a white unicorn, an orc-
captain.. just stuff that got close.

Another great thing about rangers which I find makes them so great is
that they can learn the identify spell quite well.

